text Fidelity: a screenshot comes back pixel for pixel; a photo under positioned, labelled nodes comes back with 0 differing pixels and those nodes take input; a figure drawn by another rasterizer, rebuilt from primitives, differs on 0.62% of pixels at anti-aliased edges. The engine reproduces Chromium's layout of the same stylesheet within 2 px on every box. @17,802,694,81
h2 Layout @17,895,694,21
table Path What @17,928,694,383
  spec/mx.md | The format: nodes, ids, geometry, buffers, lifecycle, patches, events, perception, transport
  spec/cheatsheet.md | The one-page version the MCP server sends as its instructions
  engine/mx | The core: parser, ids, patches, diff, perception
  engine/render | Layout (taffy), paint (tiny-skia, Inter bundled), spaces and primitives, the host with lifecycle and input, screen composition; builds to WebAssembly with a plain C ABI
  engine/mcp | manifest-mcp: the MCP server over stdio with a native window (winit) or --headless
  web/ | manifest.js, the JavaScript glue for the wasm build (browser and Node), the playground, the site build
  import/ | The HTML importer and its scorer
  bench/ | The corpus in every format, token accounting, reader accuracy, fidelity references, import scores, the report
  bench/pages/ | A hundred real pages imported into MX: the URL list with licences, the MX files, the index and the report
  docs/ | The overview and the A2UI v1.0 extension proposal
h2 Use it from an agent @17,1323,694,21
text cd engine && cargo build --release ./target/release/manifest-mcp # MCP over stdio; a window shows the surfaces ./target/release/manifest-mcp --headless # no window: layout, perception and look still work @17,1356,694,61
text .mcp.json registers it for Claude Code when you run Claude Code from this directory. For any other MCP client: @17,1429,694,40
text { "mcpServers": { "manifest": { "command": "/path/to/manifest/engine/target/release/manifest-mcp" } } } @17,1481,694,41
text Tools: manifest.render, patch, observe (levels 0 to 3, since=, focus=, wait=), look (a PNG of one node), dissolve. Every result starts with the user events since the last call. The agent gets the cheat sheet as the server's instructions and the spec as the resource manifest://spec. @17,1534,694,61
h2 The engine on the command line and in the browser @17,1607,694,21
text ./target/release/mxr render ../bench/corpus/dash.mx dash.png # paint (add --dark for the dark palette) ./target/release/mxr observe ../bench/corpus/funnel.mx 3 # perception from the engine's own layout ./target/release/mxr boxes ../bench/corpus/dash.mx # boxes and diagnostics as JSON cargo test --release # parity, host, stdio, paint, fidelity cargo build --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p mx-render # the engine for the browser cd ../web && npm install && node build.mjs # the site, playground included, into web/dist @17,1640,694,122
text From JavaScript, in a page or in Node: @17,1774,694,20
text import { loadManifest } from "./manifest.js"; const m = await loadManifest("mx_render.wasm"); m.render(mx); m.observe("dash", 2); m.compose(w, h, devicePixelRatio); m.click("dash", x, y); @17,1806,694,41
h2 Import a page @17,1859,694,21
text cd import && npm install node src/import.ts ../bench/corpus/dash.html --id dash # MX on stdout node src/score.ts imported.mx reference.mx import.json # recall, text runs, round trip node src/batch.ts ../bench/pages/urls.txt ../bench/pages/out # the dataset: a page record per URL @17,1892,694,61
